  "text": "Kurtosis Kurtosis Kurtosis measures how fat or thin the tails of a distribution are relative to a normal distribution . It is commonly defined as: Distributions with long tails are called leptokurtic; distributions with short tails are called platykurtic. Normal distributions have zero kurtosis.",
